 For left node we got humidity which actually led to the best highest information gain.

449
00:47:53,680 --> 00:48:01,240
 We will do it for the right hand side and we can verify by computing the information

450
00:48:01,240 --> 00:48:07,200
 gain that here taking the feature wind actually leads to highest information gain.

451
00:48:07,200 --> 00:48:12,240
 So here we take wind.

452
00:48:12,240 --> 00:48:14,480
 Now this can go on and on right.

453
00:48:14,480 --> 00:48:17,720
 So we will have to also stop growing a tree.

454
00:48:17,720 --> 00:48:22,800
 So we started with the root node, we now have multiple internal nodes, we also got some

455
00:48:22,800 --> 00:48:23,800
 leaf nodes.

456
00:48:23,800 --> 00:48:28,720
 At certain time we will have to decide that okay enough of it we just stop the process

457
00:48:28,720 --> 00:48:31,000
 of building the tree at this point.

458
00:48:31,000 --> 00:48:34,400
 So what is the stopping criteria?

459
00:48:34,400 --> 00:48:42,840
 So we stop when either the node consists of only training examples having the same level.

460
00:48:42,840 --> 00:48:52,400
 So if it has become pure, I mean there is no way we can further divide it or we have

461
00:48:52,400 --> 00:48:59,520
 although like the set has not become pure but we have tried out all possible features.

462
00:48:59,520 --> 00:49:05,000
 So there is no more features to test.

463
00:49:05,000 --> 00:49:11,120
 Third is that the decision tree starts to overfit.

464
00:49:11,120 --> 00:49:19,200
 Now this is something earlier Sabasachi was alluding in his the demonstrations that look

465
00:49:19,200 --> 00:49:26,360
 at certain time your model can also overfit like where you can do very well with your

466
00:49:26,360 --> 00:49:32,800
 training data but as soon as you hit a test data point then your accuracy start going

467
00:49:32,800 --> 00:49:33,800
 low.

468
00:49:33,800 --> 00:49:39,120
 In fact this can be checked by looking at the validation set accuracy that ideally the

469
00:49:39,120 --> 00:49:43,680
 validation set accuracy should be high like we do not want to do very well only with the

470
00:49:43,680 --> 00:49:48,720
 training data, we want to do well with the test data.

471
00:49:48,720 --> 00:49:56,120
 So now if we continue trying to fit the model so that it does very well with the training

472
00:49:56,120 --> 00:50:00,320
 data we may lose out on the test time performance.

473
00:50:00,320 --> 00:50:05,020
 So this is called overfitting and at certain point the decision tree will start to overfit

474
00:50:05,020 --> 00:50:10,800
 and we close or we stop growing the tree at that point.

475
00:50:10,800 --> 00:50:16,440
 So here if we can look at let us say this is the test accuracy and this is the validation

476
00:50:16,440 --> 00:50:21,720
 accuracy you see at certain point the test accuracy may continue to grow but the validation

477
00:50:21,720 --> 00:50:32,960
 accuracy may start dropping and at that point we should stop growing the tree further.

478
00:50:32,960 --> 00:50:37,880
 And one thing is important is that like if we want to obsess too much on purity then

479
00:50:37,880 --> 00:50:39,840
 it can lead to overfitting.

480
00:50:39,840 --> 00:50:46,800
 So we might be okay with let us say a scenario where 80% of the class levels are of one type

481
00:50:46,800 --> 00:50:52,320
 and 20% are of another type that is okay because that will help us prevent the tree from going

482
00:50:52,320 --> 00:50:53,800
 too much.

483
00:50:53,800 --> 00:51:00,720
 So it is okay to have leaf node that is not fully pure let us say that the probability

484
00:51:00,720 --> 00:51:08,440
 of red can be 3 by 8, probability of green can be 5 by 8 and we can simply take the majority

485
00:51:08,440 --> 00:51:12,500
 value and that is perfectly fine.

486
00:51:12,500 --> 00:51:20,720
 So at this moment let us just take a small break and let us convene again after 5 minutes

